<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-11-09.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="150226"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#150226" label="[15:02:26]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;[exa]&gt;: it should be possible to convert blynn to output M1 assembly and then you could do a haskell bootstrap avoiding C entirely.</span></div><div class="line" id="150257"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#150257" label="[15:02:57]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: unfornately, no I haven't had a chance to look into yet. Thank you for the reminder.</span></div><div class="line" id="151529"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#151529" label="[15:15:29]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ekaitz: congrats on the upcoming kid. (Just remember the work can wait, the kid definitely can't)</span></div><div class="line" id="151558"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#151558" label="[15:15:58]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: hopefully with his help i'll be able to make more work in less time later hehe</span></div><div class="line" id="151605"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#151605" label="[15:16:05]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">thank you</span></div><div class="line" id="151607"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#151607" label="[15:16:07]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">:)</span></div><div class="line" id="151804"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#151804" label="[15:18:04]">&lt;kpg&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Hi</span></div><div class="line" id="151845"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#151845" label="[15:18:45]">&lt;kpg&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Has anyone tried to bootstrap Kotlin the language?</span></div><div class="line" id="151929"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#151929" label="[15:19:29]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ekaitz: it'll be about 8 years (from what I heard) before you can get them up to speed in software engineering to be able to help.</span></div><div class="line" id="152006"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#152006" label="[15:20:06]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">:)</span></div><div class="line" id="152038"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#152038" label="[15:20:38]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">kpg: i think some guix people did, julien i think</span></div><div class="line" id="152107"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#152107" label="[15:21:07]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">kpg: i think the irc nickname is roptat</span></div><div class="line" id="152258"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#152258" label="[15:22:58]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">kpg: as I understand it you need to build openjdk-8-jdk and openjdk-11-jdk before you can bootstrap kotlin (and the path for that is in guix)</span></div><div class="line" id="152349"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#152349" label="[15:23:49]">&lt;kpg&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ekaitz: thanks</span></div><div class="line" id="152354"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#152354" label="[15:23:54]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">openjdk is easy to build</span></div><div class="line" id="152357"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#152357" label="[15:23:57]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">or relatively easy</span></div><div class="line" id="152410"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#152410" label="[15:24:10]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(especially since it is after GCC)</span></div><div class="line" id="152419"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#152419" label="[15:24:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it's the further java stuff later that is hard, e.g. maven</span></div><div class="line" id="152427"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#152427" label="[15:24:27]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">i think kotlin requires several versions to be build in chain</span></div><div class="line" id="152446"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#152446" label="[15:24:46]">&lt;kpg&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I saw kotlin 0.5.1 required the jetbrains jdk... haven't tried if it will work with the common oracle/openjdk.</span></div><div class="line" id="152529"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#152529" label="[15:25:29]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">kpg: it is always possible for specific versions of a language to become &quot;unbootstrappable&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="152557"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#152557" label="[15:25:57]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">then someone has a bunch of work to do to fix that. (Like we had with Bison)</span></div><div class="line" id="152713"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#152713" label="[15:27:13]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; hmm, main guix tree doesn't seem to have kotlin</span></div><div class="line" id="152719"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#152719" label="[15:27:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but maybe there was some work somewhere</span></div><div class="line" id="152724"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#152724" label="[15:27:24]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I seem to recall somebody building some old version</span></div><div class="line" id="153005"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#153005" label="[15:30:05]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">dude i'm pretty sure somebody worked on this</span></div><div class="line" id="153008"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#153008" label="[15:30:08]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ok, found the repo <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/ebourg/kotlin-bootstrapping">https://github.com/ebourg/kotlin-bootstrapping</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="153039"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#153039" label="[15:30:39]">&lt;ekaitz&gt;</a></span><span class="message">aaah yeah there it is, roptat is there in the bottom</span></div><div class="line" id="153109"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#153109" label="[15:31:09]">&lt;kpg&gt;</a></span><span class="message">great find, thank you stikonas</span></div><div class="line" id="153506"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#153506" label="[15:35:06]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: as for bootstrap seeds I just spotted extra 0 in the comment, need to remove that</span></div><div class="line" id="153519"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#153519" label="[15:35:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">#:write ; (0x80480A08) should be #:write ; (0x80480A8) I think</span></div><div class="line" id="153812"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#153812" label="[15:38:12]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: thank you for working to help shrink the root seeds.</span></div><div class="line" id="153823"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#153823" label="[15:38:23]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah, let me push an update first</span></div><div class="line" id="153825"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#153825" label="[15:38:25]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">just a comment update</span></div><div class="line" id="154000"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154000" label="[15:40:00]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: ok pushed</span></div><div class="line" id="154031"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154031" label="[15:40:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: anyway, most of the work was done by goldstein before</span></div><div class="line" id="154037"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154037" label="[15:40:37]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I just ported it to x86_64</span></div><div class="line" id="154104"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#154104" label="[15:41:04]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">benefits of learning as a community ^_^</span></div><div class="line" id="154107"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154107" label="[15:41:07]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">for x86, I just switched to a shorter mov instruction (1 byte)</span></div><div class="line" id="154111"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154111" label="[15:41:11]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">+ 8 byte hack with the headers</span></div><div class="line" id="154135"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154135" label="[15:41:35]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">for x86_64 I didn't overlap the headers though</span></div><div class="line" id="154152"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154152" label="[15:41:52]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it does work and run but probably against the spec</span></div><div class="line" id="154159"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154159" label="[15:41:59]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">at least readelf complains</span></div><div class="line" id="154247"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154247" label="[15:42:47]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">64-bit program header has a different order of the fields, so attempting to overlap them requires setting number of section headers to 1</span></div><div class="line" id="154317"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154317" label="[15:43:17]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">we can keep e_shentsize to 0, so kernel ignores non zero e_shnum</span></div><div class="line" id="154331"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154331" label="[15:43:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but that seemed a bit too hacky</span></div><div class="line" id="154344"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#154344" label="[15:43:44]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">on the other hand, on x86 it seems to all work fine</span></div><div class="line" id="185214"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#185214" label="[18:52:14]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">just found this talk by rickmasters <a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ycLdhqn5VI4">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ycLdhqn5VI4</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="190600"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#190600" label="[19:06:00]">&lt;Mikaku&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: good find and thanks for share it!</span></div><div class="line" id="195738"><span class="nick" style="color:#234e69"><a href="#195738" label="[19:57:38]">&lt;[exa]&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: true, thanks for the idea</span></div><br /></div></body></html>